        "entry_CyVJrA": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Setting Up",
            "text": "<p><strong>Assembling the Lower Handle </strong></p><p>1. Insert the lower handle into<br/>the slots on the deck.</p><p>2. Fix the lower handle using the enclosed screws.</p><p><strong>Assembling the Middle Handles </strong></p><p>3. Fit the middle and lower<br/>handles together with the wing nuts and washers specified for the middle handle, as illustrated in the instruction manual, onto both sides of the handle assembly. </p><p><strong>Assembling the Upper Handle </strong></p><p>4.  Fit the upper and lower handles together with<br/>the wing nuts and washers on both sides of the handle assembly. </p><p>5. Secure the cable against the<br/>handle frame with the supplied cable clips. </p><p><strong>Setting Up Your Preferred Cutting Height</strong></p><p>The mower comes with one  spacer pre-fitted and can be set to 4 cutting heights between 12mm and 33mm. Choose the appropriate cutting height according to the condition of your grass.</p><p>Watch the video below to see how to change the cutting height of your LawnMaster hover mower:</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
